@@ -27,7 +27,25 @@
 <!-- CARROT:AUTO:END PorterGap1 -->
 
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:BEGIN PorterGap1 -->
-<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="" -->
+<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="681e7e1becc8c4ad9a510ca1a73eeaadc280c4f5c3d8b35142e4dea8591312ac" reviewed-at="2026-10-29T09:00:00Z" -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Changes the selected Porter gap level’s lead-button deceleration threshold. Sub-100 values affect both the button target and the optional low-target cancellation lead check.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+100 means one second and 50 means 0.5 seconds. Levels are independent and changes apply immediately.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+0 removes only the time term, retaining the 7m minimum distance threshold. Separate from planner TF; does not guarantee actual following distance, braking or stopping.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END PorterGap1 -->
 
 <!-- CARROT:SETTING:END PorterGap1 -->
